Task (Phase 5, wiring): Scene and obstacle wiring (FR5, FR7, FR9)

What changed
- ModelPlacement gains castsShadow; planTown authors false for parked cars and
  true for houses; mountModel applies it to every mesh when present.
- Two tests, red first: the layout contract (every parked car says false, every
  house says true) and the renderer honouring it (meshes stop casting, keep
  receiving).

Why
- The model library sets castShadow on every mesh it prepares, so before this
  there was no way for a placement to opt out. FR7's whole premise -- cars carry
  a blob *instead of* a real shadow, to avoid six more casters in the 1024 map --
  was therefore unimplemented, and each car paid the shadow pass it was supposed
  to avoid while its blob double-darkened the same ground.

Measured (GL draws counted per frame on the running game, the same method as the
recorded 37,802-triangle / 133-draw baseline in tech-stack.md)
- No parked cars at all (temporary local edit to TOWN_MAP, reverted and verified
  with git diff --exit-code): 138 draw calls, 38,310 triangles.
- Before this fix: 245 draw calls, 59,768 triangles.
- After this fix: 171 draw calls, 51,130 triangles.
- So six cars + one blob mesh = +33 draw calls, +12,820 triangles, against the
  plan's expected +32.

